[h2]The Toxeus champions wear and wield what their slots can hold[/h2]
[list]
[*]Toxeus the Murderer, the Endless Hunt was carrying no armour at all. Not a low chance of armour, none: his chest, leg and arm slots did not exist on his record, and four more slots sat switched off. He now wears his own family of gear on all three, and the version you summon from his soul wears exactly what the one you fight wears.
[*]Toxeus the Murderer, Devourer of Blood was wielding a bow. In this engine the left hand is the shield and two handed ranged slot, and his left hand was rolling a table curated by affix rather than by class, with a bow in it on Normal and on Legendary. His off hand now takes a shield, his weapon hand is melee only, and he can no longer hold a bow in any slot on any difficulty.
[*]The same measurement turned up a defect nobody reported: his weapon hand was empty on roughly six spawns in ten, because it was rolling a table that is three quarters armour. He is now armed every spawn, carries his own Vein Render about seven spawns in ten, and carries a shield about six in seven. A shieldless spawn now and then is expected and means a Crimson Verdict piece dropped instead.
[*][b]Disclosed balance change.[/b] Moving that four piece set table out of his weapon hand and into his off hand takes each of the three wearable Crimson Verdict pieces from about 21 percent per kill to about 3.4 percent, and that table is the only place in the game they drop from. The Vein Render goes the other way, from about 21 percent to about 72 percent. This is a real farm slowdown on the three armour pieces and it is being flagged rather than buried; the restoration options are costed and waiting on a decision.
[/list]

[i]Also checked and NOT changed: the Devourer of Blood not dropping his soul. His soul is pinned at a 100 percent drop, the item resolves, there is no difficulty or rank gate, and only one record in the game carries his name, so every suspect the report named was cleared. The one odd thing about him was the hand wiring above, which is now gone. If his soul still fails to drop, say so and it moves to a channel already proven in game.[/i]

[i]Monster equipment only. No new items, no new monsters, no map changes, no chest changes, and no drop rate moved except the one stated above.[/i]

